  "findings": [
    "All four workloads finished and were saved, cold-read by exact session, and all owned processes exited. All eight accounting checks passed for every sample.",
    "The second candidate failed with 3843 file-callback application receive-queue overflows and 7624 separately counted follow-candidate/context drops. These are not ETW source losses and must not be added together.",
    "ETW events/buffers lost and decode failures were zero in all four captures. Both baseline captures and the first candidate passed the independent actor/completion oracle.",
    "The failed candidate retained two parent and two child write requests as EventLoss Unknown, with no promoted unrelated/background operations. Independent syscall/content truth still passed. Reliable target attribution was not established in this failed sample.",
    "Both candidate ETW ready/pre-stop/STOP samples reported zero cumulative source loss with no ControlTrace error. STOP and consumer join took milliseconds, not a long observed stop stall.",
    "Both candidate drain waits ended after 1500/1501 milliseconds with zero pending verified process instances and zero lifecycle-context losses, despite 19/139 source records arriving during the wait.",
    "Initial snapshot enumeration completed and did not exhaust its budget in either candidate, while identity queries still had failures and time-boundary exclusions. Completion does not mean full identity coverage.",
    "The failing candidate had lower aggregate file-callback time and lock-wait time than the passing candidate; these totals do not reveal short stalls, receiver-stage timing, drop ordering, or the historical Parallels cause.",
    "This unprofiled plan did not retain receiver/follow drop-reason or stage profiles. Candidate record high-water reached 2048; byte high-water was 2218701 of 8388608. Capacity pressure is observed, but counts cannot be assigned to a specific drop reason or receiver phase from these aggregates.",
    "No new live run, relaxed gate, merge, or prerelease follows this failure. The frozen package is diagnostic only; WPF acceptance was skipped by the source-comparison gate."
  ],
